# Ignore everything by default, then whitelist the authored config.
#
# WHY AN ALLOWLIST: this directory is mostly harness runtime state (projects/,
# plugins/, file-history/, session-env/, history.jsonl, jobs/, paste-cache/,
# debug/, .credentials.json). None of that is versionable and some of it is
# secret, so the safe default is to ignore everything and name the exceptions.
#
# CONSEQUENCE, read before deleting anything here: only the paths listed below
# are recoverable from git. skills/, hooks/, settings.json and .claude/ are NOT
# tracked, so removing a file in those is irreversible. Check `git ls-files`
# before you rm.
*

# Keep this file
!.gitignore

# Authored config, tracked and therefore recoverable
!commands/
!commands/**
!context/
!context/**
!playbooks/
!playbooks/**
!CLAUDE.md
